Subject: Trace lockstep state for network desync hunting
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a

Diagnostic only, under MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_LOCKSTEP_TRACE. When
MSCHARGED_RNG_TRACE names a file, every change of the shared network random
seed is written with the module offsets of its callers, and every simulation
step writes its frame number, the ball and the ten players (positions and
velocities as float bit patterns), the synchronized input of each network
player, the state of every fielder and team AI script machine, and the
result of every fuzzy AI script function, with the stack that opened each
script block. Diffing two machines' files finds the first step and value in
which a lockstep game diverges. Without the variable nothing is written.

diff --git a/include/Game/NetworkRandomSeed.h b/include/Game/NetworkRandomSeed.h
index 7df5bec..ef2e162 100644
--- a/include/Game/NetworkRandomSeed.h
+++ b/include/Game/NetworkRandomSeed.h
@@ -9,4 +9,13 @@ u32 GetNetworkRandomSeed();
 void SetNetworkRandomSeed(u32 seed);
 void OnInputSessionReset();
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_LOCKSTEP_TRACE)
+// Lockstep trace (MSCHARGED_RNG_TRACE): a game frame marker and raw float
+// state, written next to the random draws so two machines can be diffed.
+void TraceNetworkFrame(u32 frame);
+void TraceNetworkFloats(const char* label, int index, const float* values, int count);
+void TraceNetworkWords(const char* label, int index, const u32* values, int count);
+void TraceNetworkStack(const char* label);
+#endif
+
 #endif // GAME_NETWORK_RANDOM_SEED_H
